WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.534
Turning a policy on is the moment
a production job can stop,

2
00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.856
so the code asks for five things at once,

3
00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:09.775
or the ring stays held in report-only
with the reason written down.

4
00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.725
The security chief's
decision must mark the ring.

5
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:15.638
The change must explicitly
allow enforcement.

6
00:00:15.638 --> 00:00:19.162
A reviewed sign-in summary
must be cited by its hash.

7
00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:21.413
That summary must show the ring ready.

8
00:00:21.413 --> 00:00:24.451
And every earlier ring
must already be enforced.

9
00:00:24.451 --> 00:00:27.808
Exclusions are allowed,
but each one has an owner,

10
00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:32.830
a reason and an end date, and it drops
out by itself when that date arrives.
